        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Naples</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 750 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">A Greek settlement called Parthenope was established on the coast in the 8th century BCE, and in the 6th century BCE it was refounded as Neapolis, in 507 BCE by Cumaean aristocrats expelled by the tyrant Aristodemus, as one account dates it.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Gulf of Naples</a> on the western coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-vesuvius">Mount Vesuvius</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campi-flegrei">Phlegraean Fields</a>, in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A Greek colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-graecia">Magna Graecia</a>; its alliance with and later absorption by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-naples">Duchy of Naples</a>; capital of the Kingdom of Naples and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> painters and the opera of the 17th and 18th centuries; the university founded in 1224; the Four Days of Naples of 1943</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Naples is the capital of the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> and the third-largest city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and its historic centre has been a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> since 1995.</span></div>
